        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-27T20:42:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>One of the things that got me jumping up and down is when they said Targoth was making something with Oblivaeon's energy \"and let the energy shape what it wanted to be\"</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>NO! Nononononono, No! That is the worse plan, that is the absolute worst plan. Oblivaeon seems to have been mostly sentient energy, you don't let something that powerful and dangerous choose its own form. And we know it ended up as Sentient Energy... AND HE LEFT IT BEHIND ON ITS OWN!</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>IF it turns out to be a hero, that is amazing and I'm fascinated by the possiblity (any DBZ fan who remebers Uub?) but 99% likelihood that he just unleashed a new and dangerous villain into the mix.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Why would you do this Targoth, you were on a path of acceptance before this.</p>",
